<title>USA: U.S. August farm prices -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. August farm prices -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA reported average prices farmers received in August, based on prices at mid-month and compared to entire months of July 1996 and August 1995:</p>
<p> (Dlrs/Bu)-- Aug  96   July 96   Aug  95</p>
<p>  All Wheat   4.51     4.73	4.26</p>
<p>	 Corn   4.50     4.43	2.63</p>
<p>   Soybeans   7.71     7.62	5.83</p>
<p>(Dlrs/CWT)--</p>
<p>    Sorghum   6.56     6.61	4.65</p>
<p>   All Hogs  59.80    58.70     48.60</p>
<p>Average Farm Prices, cont.--</p>
<p>		    Aug  96   July 96   Aug  95</p>
<p>(Dlrs/CWT)--</p>
<p>	  Calves   58.80     56.80     70.90</p>
<p>(Cents/Lb) --</p>
<p>	Broilers    41.5	41.0     37.4</p>
<p> Upland Cotton    74.3	76.2     72.6</p>
<p>Note - Current month broiler prices are based on prices received for the entire month, while upland cotton prices are based on sales for the first half of the month.</p>
</text>
